# Test vectors ported from FerrumFIX / fefix (https://github.com/ferrumfix/ferrumfix).
# Copyright Filippo Neysofu Costa and contributors. Licensed under MIT OR Apache-2.0.
# Upstream has no NOTICE file (and the cloned snapshot has no LICENSE files at its root;
# the license is declared in Cargo.toml). '|' is SOH; the example tests themselves use '|' as the
# decoder separator, and their checksums are computed as if '|' were SOH.
#
# The snapshot (commit ca2bbe4 "Initial public release snapshot") does not contain the crates/
# directory, so the tagvalue decoder unit tests (crates/fefix/src/tagvalue/...) are not available.
# Only the workspace tests/ crate and the #[test] fn run() wrappers in examples/ were ported.
# examples/10_encode_new_order_single has a message only in a comment (not asserted); skipped.
# Upstream decoders in these tests either disable checksum verification or accept the message
# anyway; where the CheckSum is wrong we keep the vector as validate expect=error.

